                        "review": "A poorly developed, unoptimized game that looks like it was pulled out from the early 2000s. The about section and the description of Veritex looks like it was written by a 10 year old. No tutorial or instructions for the controls, and how to play. Many bugs exist in the game, from spawning in air/water, to getting stuck in objects on the map … this game is an utter nightmare.  \n\nI remember seeing another review complaint about having their level completely reset after an update and I feel bad for him/her. That is one of the glaring issues this game has. The audio was also a disappointment. You can’t year anything else but your character’s own annoying breathing.  \n\nVeritex will never meet up to the competitors of games like Rust, and its standards as a survival game are even lower than other Indie Survival games, like Salt. Because it is still in Early-Access, I do not recommend playing this game for now.",
